<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.2.6: Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00396</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.2.6: Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a3aa1435-9bb3-4b88-8103-7dc057f83552</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Write a system of equations from tables of values and graphs. </item>
  <item> Graph systems of equations by hand. </item>
  <item> Estimate real-world solutions by graphing systems of equations. </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 2.2.1: Interpreting Graphs of Systems of Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you looked at a graph of a system of equations and thought about what you noticed and wondered. You then estimated the \(y\)-intercept and slope of each equation that was graphed. </item>
  </list>
  <item> 2.2.2: Writing Systems of Equations from Tables </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you created a table of values for a given situation, then wrote a system of equations from two tables of values. </item>
    <item> 2.2.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 2.2.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 2.2.3: Graphs of Systems of Equation </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you wrote a system of equations from a graph, then worked backward to graph a system of equations by hand given the equations. </item>
    <item> 2.2.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 2.2.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 2.2.4: Systems of Equations in the Real-World </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you wrote a system of equations for a given situation, then graphed the system and estimated the solution from the graph. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list>
  <item> 2.2.5: Practice </item>
</list>
</section>
</content>
